Spec: ServiceContextServiceScript

Platform: Rhai script library (vynil-core 0.7.7 engine)

Purpose:
  The `context_service` slot ./context.sdd runs right after minting the `namespace` map:
    @template stamps the three static block keys (`ha`, `use_backup`, `name`), @run then reads
    the instance's `Namespace` object and overlays its `vynil.solidite.fr/`-prefixed
    annotations into the same map, JSON-decoded. This read is the single cluster touch of the
    whole context build and it stays on the live lane: `agent template service` lands on
    @template (a `template` fn exists, so @import_template never falls back) and no engine k8s
    call happens. Both fns mutate and return the same context map.

Exposes:
  @template(@instance, @context) — offline twin, chosen by the three-arg @import_template of
    ./context.rhai on the template lane; writes the static triple, zero k8s calls.
  @run(@instance, @context) — live twin, chosen by @import_run on the install, delete and
    `agent package test` lanes: @template first, then the guarded Namespace annotation
    overlay; returns the map.
  No other @fn; the module body is the two @fn declarations only (slot contract frozen in
    ./context.sdd Returns item 5).

Accepts:
  @instance — the injected @Dynamic ./context.rhai forwards (typed CR live, the synthesized
    `#{metadata: {name, namespace}}` map offline, the mock in /agent/src/testing/handler.sdd).
    Direct reads: `.metadata.namespace` twice only — the `name` stamp and the @get argument.
  @context — the running orchestrator map. Reads: `cluster.ha` (boolean always set by
    ./../lib/build_context.sdd on both lanes: agent.yaml value or `nodes.len() > 1`).
    Precondition: `context.namespace` is the map ./context.sdd minted immediately before this
    slot (maintenance pair present), never replaced by a `()` or non-map at slot time.

Returns:
  `context` — last expression of both fns, the same map object mutated in place (the
    orchestrator's map-guard rebind is ceremonial). New keys inside `namespace`:
    `ha` — verbatim copy of `context.cluster.ha`,
    `use_backup` — the boolean `false` (not a string; ./install.rhai gates the vitals backup
      branch on it),
    `name` — `instance.metadata.namespace`,
    plus @run's overlay: one key per prefixed annotation, @json_decode of the value text.
  The maintenance pair flows untouched unless an annotation overrides one of the two keys.
    @run never touches the top-level map.

Raises:
  Zero @throw statements; incidental throws split on @try placement:
    - @template raises propagate on both lanes (in @run it runs before the @try): a non-map
      `context.namespace`, a missing `context.cluster`, or a missing `instance.metadata`
      chain abort the lane run — shapes the three shipped callers satisfy.
    - The @k8s_resource("Namespace") construction is outside the @try too; its failure aborts.
    - Inside the @try: a failing @get (real kube NotFound error, or the mock-engine string
      `Failed to find Namespace {name} in the Mock database`) and the `instance.metadata.`
      read are caught → @log_warn, no re-throw, lane continues with the triple only.
    - Inside the loop: a non-JSON annotation text makes @json_decode raise; the per-key @try
      warns, writes nothing for that key, and the loop continues with the next key.

Handles:
  Missing object (no namespace mock, NotFound cluster): the whole guarded block degrades to
    one @log_warn line — stock mock-engine tests exercise exactly this string branch.
  `ns.metadata.annotations` absent or `()`: the `type_of(annotations) == "map"` guard skips
    the loop silently.
  Both catches share one switch: `type_of(e) == "string"` logs the raw text, anything else
    goes through @json_encode first (@log_warn takes a string only).
  Annotation key equal to the bare prefix yields the `""` key and stores its decoded value
    under it. JSON `null` values land `()` under the key.

Must:
  Stamp the triple in @template on every lane, in this assignment order: `ha` copied from
    `context.cluster.ha`, `use_backup` literal `false` always (a prior value under the key is
    clobbered), `name` from `instance.metadata.namespace`.
  Run the overlay after the triple: same-named annotations win over `ha`/`use_backup`/`name`
    and the maintenance pair — last writer is the annotation (that is the customization
    surface: an annotation can flip `use_backup` back to `true`).
  Select annotations by the literal key prefix `"vynil.solidite.fr/"` via @starts_with, and
    derive the namespace key with the Rhai string @remove — substring removal of every
    occurrence of the prefix text, not a leading-position trim.
  Decode each selected value with @json_decode inside its own @try — one bad value loses its
    own key, never the batch.
  Degrade every guarded-path failure to @log_warn (never @throw, never an instance
    `set_status_` call, never a second k8s call) and return `context` unchanged-but-stamped.
  Preserve the key spellings `ha`, `use_backup`, `name` and the prefix literal — readers are
    ./install.rhai (`namespace.use_backup`), ./../lib/backup_context.rhai (@run reads
    `namespace.ha` for the Job memory env) and the template renders of `namespace.name`.

Must not:
  Write anywhere outside `context.namespace` — the top-level context gains no key here.
  Read cluster state on the @template path (the offline lane must stay engine-call-free).

Depends on:
  vynil-core 0.7.7 script surface (registered behind /common/src/rhaihandler.sdd):
    @k8s_resource + @K8sGeneric @get (cluster-scope, one-arg), @json_decode/@json_encode,
    @type_of, @log_warn, array @filter, map @keys, string @starts_with and the `string_more`
    substring @remove.
  ./../lib/build_context.sdd — provides-and-shape authority for `cluster.ha` (read-through).
  ./context.rhai — sole caller through the slot shims; slot ordering is that contract.

References:
  ./context.sdd — Returns item 5 names this file's additions; the `namespace` mint before
    the slot and the map-guard after it.
  /agent/src/template/service.sdd — pins the offline outcome: `name` = instance namespace,
    `use_backup` `false`, `ha` from `cluster.ha`.
  ./install.sdd — `namespace.use_backup` reader; ./../lib/backup_context.sdd —
    `namespace.ha` reader.

Scenario: offline template stamps the block with zero cluster calls
  Given the /agent/src/template/service.sdd synthesized instance and the freshly minted
    maintenance map
  When @template(@instance, @context) runs
  Then `namespace` holds `ha` = the profile's `cluster.ha` boolean, `use_backup` `false`,
    `name` the instance namespace, the maintenance keys survive, and no engine call is made
  Covered from the lane side by /agent/src/template/service.sdd namespace-block scenarios

Scenario: live annotation overlay merges and overrides
  Given a mocked engine holding a `Namespace` object in the instance namespace, whose
    `metadata.annotations` carry `vynil.solidite.fr/use_backup` JSON text `true` and
    `vynil.solidite.fr/maintenance_start_hour` JSON text `"3"`
  When @run(@instance, @context) runs
  Then `use_backup` is `true` (annotation beat the false stamp), `maintenance_start_hour` is
    the string `"3"` (annotation beat the minted `"0"`), `ha`/`name` keep the stamped values
  No mapped test

Scenario: one malformed annotation loses only its key
  Given a mocked `Namespace` in the instance namespace whose `metadata.annotations` carry
    `vynil.solidite.fr/ha` with the invalid JSON text `yes` and `vynil.solidite.fr/name`
    with the JSON string text `"\"renamed\""`
  When @run(@instance, @context) runs
  Then @log_warn reports the @json_decode failure, `ha` stays the cluster boolean, `name`
    becomes `renamed`, the run completes
  No mapped test

Scenario: namespace object absent degrades to a warning
  Given the stock /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs mock set (ServiceInstance only, no
    Namespace)
  When @run(@instance, @context) runs
  Then the string @type_of branch calls @log_warn with the raw text, no annotation key is
    written, a map is returned
  Indirectly covered by @service_context_builds_context_from_instance (lane-completes side)

Tasks:
  [ ] Extend /agent/tests/rhai_lifecycle.rs mocks: add a `Namespace` object with prefixed
      annotations to pin overlay/override, per-key JSON isolation and the no-annotations
      silent skip (today the get always fails on the mock string, so the loop is untested).
  [?] `@remove` strips every occurrence of the prefix text, so a key containing the prefix
      mid-string gets a multi-segment name — decide keep vs leading-only trim before any
      longer-lived annotation naming guide ships.
  [?] The `_` catch branch @json_encodes the caught dynamic and that call itself raising
      would escape the last @try and abort the lane — decide whether the error switch needs
      a @log_warn fallback on the `${e}` interpolation.
  [?] The overlay intentionally reaches the maintenance pair and `name`: confirm the
      override surface is the contract rather than restricting settable keys.

Done when:
  The four scenarios have mapped tests or recorded decisions, the key spellings cross-check
    against ./context.sdd Returns item 5 and the two reader specs, and `specdd lint` is green.
